Package: fieldborders
Type: Package
Title: Agricultural Field Boundaries from Sentinel-2 Time Series
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8401-472X")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", role = "aut"))
Description: Delineates agricultural fields from Sentinel-2 image time series.
    The temporal boundary contrast method ranks spectral bands and indices by how
    differently they change through the season on the two sides of a field border
    and inside one field, learns an edge map from the selected contrasts and a
    cropland map from per-pixel temporal statistics, and turns both maps into
    field objects by marker-controlled watershed. The maps can be fused with the
    class probabilities of deep segmentation models such as the Fields of The World
    PRUE models, which can be run from R. Functions cover monthly Sentinel-2 download
    from a STAC catalogue, training with reference polygons, pretrained models,
    threshold tuning, polygon export, object-level accuracy assessment compatible
    with the Fields of The World benchmark, and maps of the results.
